values ('a1b2c3d4-5e6f-4b40-9d90-0e1f2a3b4c00', 'medieval-literature', 'Medieval Literature', 'Medieval Literature introduces students to major Old and Middle English texts, genres, languages, and manuscript cultures from the Anglo-Saxon period through the later Middle Ages. Students read heroic poetry, elegy, romance, Chaucer, allegory, religious writing, drama, prose, women''s visionary writing, and Arthurian tradition while learning how manuscript transmission, multilingual England, performance, translation, and modern reception shape interpretation. The course combines close reading with historical context, basic Middle English reading skills, material-text awareness, and research methods.');

